{"name":"March Breeze","hex":"#e3dacf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"march","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A formal, rhythmic way of walking, used especially by soldiers, by bands, and in ceremonies.","A journey so walked."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To walk with long, regular strides, as a soldier does.","To cause someone to walk somewhere."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/march"},{"term":"breeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, gentle wind.","Any activity that is easy, not testing or difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move casually, in a carefree manner.","To blow gently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"March","blocks":[{"text":"March is the third month of the year in both the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. In the Northern Hemisphere, the meteorological beginning of spring occurs on the first day of March. The March equinox on the 20 or 21 marks the astronomical beginning of spring in the Northern Hemisphere and the beginning of autumn in the Southern Hemisphere, where September is the seasonal equivalent of the Northern Hemisphere's March."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March","wikidata":"Q110"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_mars.jpg/500px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_mars.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_mars.jpg/500px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_mars.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"March, from the Très Riches Heures du Duc de Berry, a book of prayers to be said at canonical hours","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALes_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_du